  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 405.12 Calculation of Peak Flow for CWSs",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 405.12 Calculation of Peak Flow for CWSs. Peak flow shall be calculated as design flow times the multiplier in Table 405-1 with the number of residential-equivalent units being calculated in accordance with Env-Dw 405.06(a)(9)a.:\n\nTable 405-1: Peak Flow\n\nNumber of Residential Service Connections or Residential-Equivalent Units | Peaking Factor (Peak Flow / Design Flow)\n\nLess than 50 | 10\n\n50 to 99 | 9\n\n100 to 149 | 7\n\n150 to 199 | 5\n\nGreater than 200 | 4\n\nSource. #14158, eff 12-25-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html"
}
